WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.230
- [Narrator] Last year, the
auction house Christie's

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.440
sold a JPEG by the artist Beeple

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.048
for a record-breaking $69 million.

00:00:09.048 --> 00:00:11.990
- Beeple's sale hit the art
market like an earthquake.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.470
- [Narrator] For many,
the sale of this NFT

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.140
represents a revolution for the art market

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.360
since it was the first piece of art sold

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.690
by a major auction house that
does not physically exist.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:25.170
- There's this real gold rush feel

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.360
to sort of being on the ground
floor of something dynamic.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.240
And with that comes a lot of risk.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.910
And I think the art market is still trying

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.470
to figure out where this will go

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.429
but I don't think it's going anywhere.

00:00:36.429 --> 00:00:37.262
(gavel banging)

00:00:37.262 --> 00:00:38.320
- Sold to you out there online. Thank you.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.330
- [Narrator] So how are NFTs
transforming the art market?

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.900
And if this technology goes mainstream,

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.450
who stands to benefit?

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.790
- Let's give him a Cyberquad.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:51.090
- [Narrator] This is Niche Markets,

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:54.020
a series about small, lesser-known markets

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.179
that despite their size,

00:00:55.179 --> 00:00:56.490
(till clanging)

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.990
punch well above their weight.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:03.870
In 2021, the concept
of a non-fungible token

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.670
or NFT entered the zeitgeist.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.640
- NFTs in 2021 were an
incredibly important milestone.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.480
It has a really revolutionary impact

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.540
on the art business.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.320
- NFTs for me, it's a new genre of art.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.840
- Digital art has existed for decades.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.890
I think we will always think of a before

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.870
and an after in terms of NFTs.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.530
- [Narrator] NFTs are digital tokens

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.140
with vouchers of authenticity

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.540
that represent digital or
real-life art or collectibles.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.930
- An NFT is essentially a receipt

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:35.750
that you can never throw away.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:38.310
If you need proof that you own a thing,

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:41.550
an NFT is one way to
lock that down forever.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.960
- [Narrator] Although NFTs have
been around for a few years,

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.800
it wasn't until 2021
when they really began

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.900
to attract widespread attention.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:52.420
- So we are in my living room

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.890
and we're watching the
closing of the auction.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.100
- [Narrator] The artist
behind this piece of work

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.910
is Mike Winkelmann,
better known as Beeple.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:02.830
69 million.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:06.740
I think it probably means
digital art is here to stay.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.610
- [Narrator] Christie's
says the sale of "Everydays"

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.570
makes Beeple among the top three

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.580
most valuable living artists.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.420
A fact made all the more remarkable

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:17.480
since "Everydays" began bidding at $100.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:19.730
- It was truly a watershed moment.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:24.020
It introduced NFTs into
the auction world in 2021,

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.470
which was really the biggest
headline for our business.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:30.310
- For him to come in with
essentially a JPEG collage

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:33.770
and outsell Frida Kahlo and Salvador Dali,

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:35.830
I mean, the art market
couldn't wrap its head

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.940
around what we were experiencing.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.974
And it was definitely a
marker of a brand new world.

00:02:40.974 --> 00:02:42.310
(playful music)
(keys clacking)

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.710
- [Narrator] Artist Cam
Rackam spends his days

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:48.300
in his Southern California
studio creating NFTs.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.890
- I've been a artist for 18 years.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:54.070
I started dappling with
NFTs during the pandemic.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:55.200
I thought it was gonna be two weeks

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.680
and it just went on and on.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.280
I watched my art shows melt away.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.540
- [Narrator] Before the pandemic,

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.260
Rackam's income came mostly

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.640
from gallery sales and commissions.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.670
But lockdowns put him on unemployment

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.080
and forced him to pivot his business.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.940
- NFTs have massively changed my life.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:16.880
Let's give him a little
Wall Street Bull sign.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.320
I didn't plan for that or expect that.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:20.153
There we go.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:24.810
But I went from marginally
successful painter

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.950
to full-time NFT maker.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.640
- [Narrator] Rackam is the
artist behind a collection

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.340
of NFTs known as Wall Street Bulls,

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:36.900
which is comprised of
10,000 cartoon bull NFTs.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.300
- This one has a pipe,

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.150
this one has a laser eye.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.940
This one has a goatee.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:43.400
Maybe a beard.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.250
- [Narrator] Each of the
Wall Street Bull NFTs

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.130
parodies different aspects

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.380
of today's social media-fueled
retail trading culture.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:53.010
- AOC, we gave her her
famous tax the rich dress

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:55.170
and she's got commie
horns and a Bernie tattoo.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.370
- [Narrator] The collection was produced

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.850
in partnership with the team

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:01.200
behind the satirical Instagram
account Wall Street Memes,

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.240
which takes much of its inspiration

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.770
from the popular wallstreetbets subreddit

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:09.130
that was at the center of
last year's GameStop mania.

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:12.430
- We thought with being
bullish on the market,

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.150
the bull as a character
made a lot of sense to us.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.913
That's J.P. Morgan and
John D. Rockefeller.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:21.020
- [Narrator] Although the
sales that have grabbed many

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.890
of the headlines have to do
with specific works of art,

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.500
like Beeple's "Everydays" or "HUMAN ONE,"

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.730
some of the most popular
NFTs bought and sold today

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:31.090
are part of collections.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:31.923
- The really cool thing

00:04:31.923 --> 00:04:34.370
about how NFTs have really exploded

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.880
is that it's given sort of
all kinds of art a chance

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:41.100
to shake out and find its
own subcategory, right?

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.990
So you have the apes and the Dogecoins

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:47.340
and the various animal creatures.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.970
They're almost similar
to being part of a club.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.300
- [Narrator] NFT collections tend

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.310
to follow a release strategy
similar to sneaker drops.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.000
They come in limited quantities,

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.030
depend on sky-high demand

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:02.480
and stir speculative crazes
in the secondary market.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.750
- The secondary market is like...

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.530
It's probably the most beautiful part

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.670
of the NFT selling spectrum.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:11.370
- [Narrator] Thanks to a
few lines of code embedded

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:12.890
within an NFT,

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.760
artists are guaranteed a cut

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:18.690
of any and all future sales
of their work in perpetuity.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:22.740
- Now as an artist, you
can collect a royalty.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.350
As a creator, a developer,

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:28.368
you do get kind of what
you deserve finally.

00:05:28.368 --> 00:05:30.280
(playful music)

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.670
- [Narrator] Rackam told The Journal

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:34.060
that the Wall Street
Bulls collection sold out

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.680
in 32 minutes,

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.070
netting the team behind
it an initial profit

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:43.070
of $2.6 million of which
his take home was $726,000.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.160
Since the project went
live on October 27th,

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:53.160
Rackam said he's made an
additional $62,000 in royalties.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.640
- We've been in this
kind of auction house,

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:58.240
corporate contemporary
world for a very long time.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.113
NFTs are so much more democratic.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:03.483
There we go.

00:06:03.483 --> 00:06:05.990
- We come to a place where
artists have more say

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:07.750
over where their works go

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.750
and they have more, you
know, they're getting a cut

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.740
of resales and they're
knowing where everything is.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.550
I mean, certainly that
does shift the balance

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:16.470
of power a little bit

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:17.740
in the favor of the little guy

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:21.280
and of the artist as opposed
to the power brokers.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.770
- [Narrator] These new buyers

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.920
are far younger than those
who typically participate

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:27.380
in high-priced auctions.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.470
- 75% of the people who participated

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:31.020
in our NFT sales this year

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.370
were entirely new to Christie's.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.180
Our average NFT buyer's 42 years old.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.770
That's more than 10 years younger

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.510
than the buyers across categories.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:41.510
- Ahead of you in Hong Kong.

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:42.940
16 is here, thank you.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.452
- [Narrator] To cater
to this new clientele,

00:06:44.452 --> 00:06:49.320
the 255-year-old auction house
changed its payment policies.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:52.370
- We had to expedite our readiness

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.270
to accept cryptocurrency

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.790
because it was absolutely demanded by some

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.010
of the avid NFT buyers.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:00.530
And now we're delighted

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:02.730
that we're actually
accepting cryptocurrency

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.410
not only for NFT works

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:07.210
but for works across other categories.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:09.930
- The much anticipated sequel

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.450
to Beeple's first offering
here at Christie's.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:16.680
- [Narrator] In 2021, Christie's
sold around $150 million

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:20.740
in NFTs for 8% of its
contemporary art sales.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.310
- We think NFTs are here to stay.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.260
We've had great conversations
with so many artists,

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:28.430
musical artists, visual artists,

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.710
so I think the sky's the limit.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:34.040
- Here in the moment, $24 million.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.473
25 online.

